# c-script / Link (.link) Developer Guide for AI & Cursor

You are developing with **c-script** (file extension `.link`, CLI `linkc`), a high-performance backend language designed specifically for End-to-End Type Safety with TypeScript frontends.

## Key Syntax Reference

### 1. Types & Data Structures
<!-- linkc:part -->
```rust
// Basic types: Int, Float, Int64, String, Bool, Timestamp, Void
// Postfix collections: T[] or Map<K, V> or Tuples (A, B)
// Nullable: T? (maps to T | null)

type User = {
  id: Int,
  name: String,
  email: String,
  role: Role,
  createdAt: Timestamp,
  avatar?: String,
}

enum Role {
  Admin,
  Member,
  Guest,
}

enum Result<T, E> {
  Ok { value: T },
  Err { code: Int, message: E },
}
```

### 2. Database Definition (`db { ... }`)
<!-- linkc:part -->
```rust
db {
  users: User[],
}
// Operations: db.users.all(), db.users.find(id), db.users.insert(row),
// db.users.applyPatch(id, patch), db.users.delete(id), db.users.findWhere(predicate)
```

### 3. Services & Streaming
<!-- linkc:part -->
```rust
service Users {
  rpc list(limit: Int = 20) -> User[] {
    db.users.all()
  }

  @authenticated
  rpc me() -> User? {
    db.users.find(1)
  }

  @requires(Role.Admin)
  rpc remove(id: Int) -> Bool {
    db.users.delete(id)
  }

  stream watch() -> User {
    while true {
      db.users.subscribe()
    }
  }
}
```

### 4. Built-in Testing
<!-- linkc:part -->
```rust
test "insert and retrieve" {
  let user = db.users.insert(User {
    id: 0,
    name: "John",
    email: "john@example.com",
    role: Role.Member {},
    createdAt: now(),
  });
  assert(user.id > 0, "ID assigned by SQLite");
}
```

## CLI Commands
- Build TS contracts: `linkc build <file.link> <outdir>`
- Run test runner: `linkc test <file.link>`
- Start server: `linkc serve <file.link> <port>`
- Dev mode with hot reload: `linkc dev <file.link> <outdir> [port]`
- Format code: `linkc fmt <file.link>`
- Lint code: `linkc lint <file.link>`
- Generate docs: `linkc doc <file.link>`
